cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RACRP: deriving the serverless keep-alive window from a cost model"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Goyal
    given-names: Parth
    alias: parthgoyal974
    affiliation: "Vellore Institute of Technology"
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Saanvi
    alias: saanvi3605
    affiliation: "Vellore Institute of Technology"

# Both authors contributed to this work jointly. The repository is hosted under
# a shared organisation so that neither account is privileged over the other.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ColdStart-Lab/RACRP"
url: "https://github.com/ColdStart-Lab/RACRP"
abstract: >-
  The keep-alive policy deployed in Azure Functions reads its warm window off
  two fixed percentiles of a per-application idle-gap histogram. This work
  shows that the window can instead be derived, by minimising the expected cost
  of the warm window jointly over its pre-warm offset and its keep-alive length,
  which replaces the percentile with the price of a cold start in GB-minutes.
  Evaluated on the Azure Functions 2019 trace at matched memory cost, the
  derived window reduces cold starts by a median 78.8% against the deployed
  policy and 67.6% against a baseline strengthened to tune both of its
  percentiles. The identical optimiser given another application's history
  scores -427%, establishing that the gain requires each application's own past.
keywords:
  - serverless
  - cold start
  - keep-alive
  - optimal stopping
  - Azure Functions
license: MIT
